A||||18||flexableface||poll!! wild adventures||||10||
Z||000000||flexableface||11-13-2000||10:52 AM||||what is the wildest thing you have done in a fiero or seen someone do?||||reg||10
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-13-2000||02:17 PM||||a "FRIEND" wanted to drive my nitrous SE. he JUST a week prior got a new 380(rwhp) 351 installed in his truck so i was like SURE.. here are the keys. he hands me his and i explain the clutch is tricky and the clutch WILL NOT slip don't try and make it. ok, we made it out of the Steak and Shake parking lot and down to the end of the road where there is a red light and a right hand turn with our own lane to merge into US HWY41 traffic (5 lane hwy) i'm slowing down and readying to yeild as my "FRIEND" shifts in to 3rd and flips the nos switch and stomps on it. dumps the clutch and the car breaks loose spins clockwise facing into on comming traffic, tires spinning about 50mph+ the wrong direction BILLOWING the smoke and stinch of 245s. with a HUGE cloud of tire smoke i'm DEEP on his brakes, his monsterous 33x12.5 TSLs howl to a stop in the center of the lanes trying to block traffic.. not probly 2 seconds later i see the nitrous light come back on in the car he pops it in 1st and stomps the gas looking like Luke Duke spins it around and hauls @$$ about 200 yards to the taco bell parking lot and gets out. hands me the keys through the truck window and shaking terribly quivvers "i'm sorry, man... i'm going home."  he was really shaken up.. and so was i & my girlfriend. we just KNEW it was the last time we'd ever see John and my SE in one piece again.  He never in the 2 years after asked to drive the car again... <P>his waste of band width. <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/littlered351/stuckinarutindex.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/littlered351/stuckinarutindex.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>"Fondue forks for everybody"<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||11-13-2000||06:45 PM||||Jeez Trav, the SE has had a hard life!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>This isn't nearly as spectacular, BUT... I was coming out of the Target parking lot onto a semi-major intersection with my old GT(now 1FST2M6's.)  The pavement was a little damp, but it wasn't raining(I thought it was pretty dry.) I was making a left hand turn through the intersection and felt like being cool, so I gave it full throttle as I was just coming out of the turn and totally lost it!  It was freakish the way it got away from me(too used to the handling of my '94Z) and I spun a complete 360.  I came to a complete stop(heart pounding) and looked around myself sheepishly, then SLOWLY went home and crawled into a hole.  I felt like such a moron...  <P>The MOST fun I've had in a Fiero was autocrossing in my friends 3.1 SE and losing another friends Firebird on the parking ramps at 1am in the morning.||||reg||1
Z||000003||zeusrekning||11-13-2000||07:45 PM||||I was coming down I26 in the rain one morning trying to keep up with my g/f's brother when i see his truck tail lights out my pass. side window.<BR>i relize i'm spinning. I spin off the interstate into a ditch about 25 yards down the hill. With my headlights pointiong into the trees no body stopped for about 30 minutes. It was dark and you could not miss the lit up trees. <BR>Oh i still drive the car be both madit with no bad scratches.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||11-13-2000||08:20 PM||||In heavy rain on I-675, spun & hit the concrete wall 3 times.  Right in front of the Astrodome.  Nobody stopped to see if I was alright.<P>BTW, have you seen these?... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003625.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003625.html</A> <BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||11-14-2000||01:05 PM||||Not exactly a "wild adventure," but all this spinning in the rain stuff reminds me...<P>Street was wet.  Was turning left (south) from a stop, shifted into 2nd in the middle of the turn, let out the clutch normally.  Immediately did a 180+ degree spin and ended up facing north, in the N-bound left turn lane.  Fortunately, there were no other cars/people around, so no damage.<BR>"Hmmm, how'd that happen?"<P>At that point, realized the engine was idling really fast. So, nursed it home that way, thinking, "Great, I don't know anything about these new computerized cars."  At home, discovered that the PCV hose had fallen off the bottom of the upper plenum, letting <B>lots</B> of air in.  Must have fallen off right in the middle of that turn (BTW, the car had the OE Eagle GuTs tires  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Reinstalled the PCV hose - with a <B>clamp</B> on it this time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000006||ur2biteme||11-14-2000||07:03 PM||||back when i had my mustang, i had a friend that who swore up and down that i couldnt freak him out driving.  (this was a few years ago, dont flame me please) his dad used to drive very crasy (cut across 5 lanes of traffic to make an exit, just so he could buy a pie).  well, i'm going on one of those slow spiraling on-ramps when i decide to freak him out.  no traffic for miles (late at night) i break the back end loose and spin a 540 across the 3 lanes and stop the car next to the retaining wall (6 lane freeway).  needless to say, he no longer made that claim.  <P>in my fiero, well, it wasnt intentional.  i was hauling a$$ down a back road i almost always drive down to unwind.  i was taking it a little faster than usual, late at night.  the last turn before i get to the highway goes up an incline, at the crest of the hill, it cuts right slightly.  well, i was going about 95 (i guess, you know the damn speedometers) when i crested the hill, with what i thought was the gradual turn to the right.  well, i oversteered a little because of the speed, and the back end swung around, kept the car sideways, almost corrected it straight, the back end swung the other direction, then back to the left and into a ditch.  i know there was a 360 in there somewhere, just not sure where.  lol.  got out, inspected, drove it since.  well, untill the tranny blew a few weeks ago.  but this incident was almost 9 months ago.<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000007||Patrick's Dad||11-16-2000||12:42 AM||||Hmm, all these speed stories. Judging by the topic, I expected naked body stories....<P>I worked at a small HiFi chain in eastern MA about 15 years ago. In fact, excluding the owner, I think that I am the only person to have sold equipment out of all six of the stores at the height of the chain's success (They are still around, but only one store.).<P>I was spending a week at the Saugus store (North of Boston), as the manager was on vacation. The AM and I closed the store, then ran the deposit to the bank. We said our good nights, and I attempted, in the rain, to find the little street that went under Route 1 to head Southbound, to home. (Note: Even though it's raining, and I am in a 5sp Duke Fiero, there is no speed, nor spinning, to follow.) I skirted the parking lot, as I thought that I remembered Jim doing the night before, and found the opening. Or so I thought. I climbed a short hill that I wasn't sure that I remembered, and the next thing I know, I was staring into the window of someone's house. My trek had taken me right into someone's back yard. I eased the car backward from whence I had come. I then decided that the best thing for me to do was to go up Rt1 North until I hit a place to turn.<P>Sorry for the anticlimax. I put BFG Euro TA's on it, and the d**n car didn't slide when I tried to avoid hitting a guy who stopped hard in front of me, while another guy was coming hard on the left. I just remember jerking the wheel hard to the left, then hard to the right, and I was in the next lane, unscathed. The reason I didn't tell that story, is that I thought is was funnier to be in someone's back yard. Maybe it isn't. I just know that it's quarter to one in the morning, and my baby girl is coughing herself awake....<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000008||2xsess||11-16-2000||01:34 AM||||Ok, here's my little story. It was in my 2nd Fiero an 84SE 4spd. I had only had this one for about a week. I was living in PA at the time. After having driven my 1st 84 through 9" of snow and all kinds of rain I thought I knew these cars. I was on my way home form work one evening and in was lightly raining. The road home was a steady slow incline with small bends and curves, nothing too serious. I wasn't speeding, which was rare for me at the time. As I crested the one uprise the back of the car swung arround, I tried to correct it without sucess. I ended up doing two 360 and bumping the embankment with the nose. When I came to a stop I slowly pulled up to a pull off and got out on shaky knees to check for damage. As I was walking around checking the car (thankfully no damage)my father drove down the hill. He stopped and asked me what happened. I told him and he said "oh, ok well we're heading to the store, see you later" and off he went. <P>Sorry so long  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||11-16-2000||01:56 AM||||Well, I just had my own wild and not so good adventure about a half-hour ago.  In fact, I'm still shaking....<P>We finally got our first real snow here in minnesota, and even though the highways weren't too slippery I was taking it easy.  Everything was fine until I got to my off-ramp.  I saw that it was pretty slushy, so I tried to slow down before I hit the slush.  Didn't get quite slow enough, though, and as soon as I hit it I felt the rear end coming around.  The next thing I remember is watching the diamond marker sign slam into my passenger side mirror, and hearing the crunch.  After some (a lot) of screamed obscenities I get out to look at the damage.. passenger side ground f/x are pretty much gone, nice notch in the pass. side door panel.  It looks like the post hit my door panel first, then took out the mirror.  <P>It could have been worse, there were 2 other marker signs behind that one, and judging from the tire tracks I missed one by a few inches.  <P>I'll be posting this as a new topic, too.. <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||11
Z||000010||fldevel||11-16-2000||12:46 PM||||i was going down US19 once *note speed limit is 65* now this is a 4 lane highway with a devider in the middle .. when there where 2 cars side by side doing anywhare between 28-40 mph talking back and forth to eachother.. i just happen to be behind them .. so i was getting a little ticked off so i waited til they got far enough apart and droped into 3rd and punched it right between them while giving a few choice gestures ...i do not advise neone to try this themselves .. this is verry dangerous and should not be attempted ... and another time i was driving my freightliner and happen to look down in a nice lookin red GT with a nice lookin topless chick driving it .. (if this female is on this forum and single my number is.... :P) well just e-mail me ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Patrick's Dad||11-16-2000||12:49 PM||||Oh, yeah. Now reading the accidentals, I actually do have a spinning story....<P>It was also in my '85 2M4, coming home from work on a snowy evening. I was going kinda slow on Rt 128N (which is also Rt 93S. Don't ask) because of a couple of minor fishtails, heading for the Rt 28 Randolph exit. However, as I neared, I noticed a statie with its lights on, behind another car which seemed to be stuck. I decided that it would be just as easy for me to come in the back way. I eased out of my line, intending to cross the highway to Rt 24S. Unfortunately, my car had a different idea. It must have hit some patch of ice, as the rear end went out, sending me into the first 360 before I even realized it. The second and third 360's came (in opposite directions) as a result of my fighting the spin. Clarity of though hit, and I let the car do what it seemed to want to do, which was to go backwards. I used the steering wheels as rudders to guide my car into the snowbank at the right side of the road. Thankfully, traffic was well behind me through this episode.<P>The statie had obviously observed this lane crossing dance, and pulled backwards out of the exit. Lights still going, he pulled up by me as I was out of the car, catching my breath and inspecting (in the dark) for damage. He yelled at me "What do you think you're doing?" I explained that the car did what it wanted until I figured out how to guide it. He told me to get out of there, then, once in our cars, he ordered over his loudspeaker to turn my lights on (I don't remember turning them off....). I crawled down 24 and all the other streets home.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||TheFiero64||11-16-2000||04:48 PM||||Well here is a story I have that happened this summer. There were 3 Fieros coming back to Cape cod mass from the Kickhill Farm swap meet in Conn. I was in the lead Jaygee79 was in the middle and Mattsfiero was tailing the end. We stopped for gas then headed back onto the highway. The sign said next exit Rt. 6. I took the exit and ended up in the middle of the woods. I said to the others this doesn't,t look like Rt. 6. So we got back on the only entrance ramp back to the highway but, The exit ended up putting us in the incorrect direction back toward Kickhill farm. We stopped at the service station and asked for directions. They said that people get stuck on that stupid exit all the time. The directions they gave us had us get off of an exit and take the backroads to Rt. 6. We were following the directions but the others thought we were still lost. They kept telling me on the CB to pull over and get more directions. I saw 3 kids standing in a parking lot and decided to pull in. I didn't see the high curb that was black and ended up fling over it. I think the Fiero went airborne. Everyone was looking at me. I thought I destroyed the undercarriage of my car. It was fine but what a scary thing that was.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. The guys in the parking lot were more amazed by seeing 3 cars that were all the same. We found out we were on the right track and got home at 11:30 PM.<P><B>P.S. Patrick's Dad,</B> I know how funny it is that 128N is also 93S. I work in Norwood and live in New Bedford. My first day up there I headed the wrong way home. I saw 128N toward Braintree/Boston or 95 south toward Providence. I said to myself It must be 95 South so I ended up having to go 95S to 495 to 24S to 140S to get back home LOL. It actually only takes like 15 min. longer. If there is a backup on the highway I go that way. If I have someone with me when I go up that way I like to confuse them by saying that 128N is 93S and turns into 95N and to go to NH we can go 128N or south and still get there   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>How dumb did that sound?<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 11-16-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000013||fropuff||11-16-2000||09:10 PM||||Probably my "wild" adventure was last Friday.  I was screwing around in the driveway, understeered a 45 degree turn going about 25, the front left tire went through the snow, was turned when I hit the pavement again.  The back came around to the right side, so I tried to get it straight.  The rear came back too fast, so it came around to the left.  I knew I was going into the trees, so I threw the wheel to the left and punched it to the floor.  It seemed to help, but I slid sideways into the trees anyway.  By looking at my marks, I see that I was about 5" from hitting a small tree with the rear, and about a foot from three trees that would have totaled out the left side.  I got pretty lucky.  I ended up with some bad scratches, but the GS-27 took them right out.  That's about the only ride I've been on in the Fiero, and it was in the frickin driveway.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Will||11-18-2000||10:44 PM||||Hehe... Where do I start?<P>I was upside-down, backwards, AIRBORNE, at 55++mph in an '87 GT once...<BR>I won't go into how I got there, but the poor '87 gave it's all to keep me safe. I walked away with scratches and kept the car for parts &lt;sniff&gt;<P>     In my next Fiero, an '86 SE V6 with 5 spd conversion, grafted '88 front suspension w/1&1/8" swaybar, completely worn out rear struts, and the original 7/8" swaybar "engineered" onto the back (that car LOVED to spin, but it sure would drift beautifully going up the mountain--I digress), I was taking a girl back from a rained out performance of The Merchant of Venice, and coming down a 270 degree onramp (onto the Capital Beltway, I think) I was going a little fast and broke the rear end loose. Tried to correct for an instant before I realized that I would be sliding into 65+mph traffic trying to controll a fishtailing car in the rain. I stomped the brakes to lock up all four wheels, did a clockwise 270 and ended up backed onto the shoulder. After a second to let the gas stop sloshing around in the tank, it started right up and I drove away.<P>I should NOT have even been THINKING about going fast with someone else in the car.<P>I was on a cruise with my local car club one day several months later. We were traversing backroads rather quickly, and I was thinking, "Something's wierd, I don't have the grip I should. What's going on?"<BR>I was on cheap tires while everyone else had the standard lowered Honda with 215/20-ZR21 tires that stuck like glue, so I was pushing pretty hard to keep up. We went over a rise with a dropoff and an IMMEDIATE right hander afterward. I got a little hairy on the turn, slid left, slid right, slid left, decided it was not reliably recoverable and induced a spin by stomping the brakes. Didn't slide off the side of the mountain, fortunately. When we got back to the RV, I checked my tire pressures, and ALL FOUR were 5 psi low. I think someone was @$%&ing with my car, with dangerous consequences.||||reg||1
Z||000015||sqoach||11-18-2000||11:04 PM||||well i have a story to tell.  nothing exciting really but newayz...me and a friend were cruising the town one misty night.  he has a 96 civic and we were just goofing around, racing at stoplights and stuff.  well, as we took off from one stoplight, he bolts out in front of me and decides he wants to cut me off.  well he hit a patch of sand in the road and spun a 180 then back around, nearly hitting my precious car.  he just stopped and looked at me for a second then we drove back to my house.  he told me he knew what he was doing, but i knew he was scared sh**less.<P>well thought i'd share a story<BR>(trying to build up my replies)<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||10
Z||000016||Cheever2||11-18-2000||11:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B>...(trying to build up my replies)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>  Honest.  I like this guy.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||sqoach||11-18-2000||11:57 PM||||hey thanks cheever.  hey, how do you do that quote thing?||||reg||1
Z||000018||Cheever2||11-19-2000||12:06 AM||||Okay, when you want to respond to some <B>specific</B> thing somebody said... do you see those 4 boxes to the right of their name on their post?  Click on the far right one IN THAT POST (the one which contains the statement to which you want to reply).  That will bring up their post.  You can use the delete key to take out parts that don't apply to whatever it is you want to address.  Then at the bottom, just add your own comments.  boy, I hope I said that right.<BR>||||reg||1
